 "notes": [
  "true mismatch = the model rejected a human label (false alarm, up to EPIC's own label noise). Its reasons are mostly 'the main action is something else': EPIC labels are atomic and overlap with what else the hands do (turning on the tap while washing), so part of this is label granularity.",
  "same_verdict_share = clips where the label and its exact reverse got the same verdict; the sign test asks whether, on the other clips, the model sided with the label more often than chance.",
  "swapped mismatch = direction errors caught; other mismatch = unrelated labels caught.",
  "Labels are short kitchen actions, EgoDex descriptions are long sentences: compare directions of effects, not exact rates."
 ]
